1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
The steadiest human hand still trembles.
About a hundred microns.

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,700
A surgical robot works at under five.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:08,800
In some operations,
that difference is everything.

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,820
Think about what that precision unlocks.

5
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,860
Reconnecting nerves thinner than a thread.

6
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,320
Preparing the delicate
structures of the eye.

7
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,520
Operating in spaces
so small and so critical

8
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:20,220
that a human tremor could cause real harm.

9
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,420
The robot doesn't eliminate the surgeon.

10
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,640
The surgeon is still guiding every move.

11
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,700
It eliminates the shake.
Turns a good hand into a perfect one.

12
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,740
This is why robotic
surgery keeps expanding

13
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,680
into more and more delicate procedures.

14
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,580
It's not about looking futuristic.

15
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,840
It's about doing things for patients
that simply weren't possible before.

16
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,580
Safely, precisely, consistently,
precision changes what is possible.

17
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,040
Medicine? You know the answer. Cratheon.
